{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"impressive-doddering-alpinegoat","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\nSurfaced while fixing `anatomical-arbored-oyster` (e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a). With the mirror sweep's collection/install errors removed, `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` now runs and fails on the non-editable macOS and floor legs:\n\n```\nAssertionError: Resolved repo_root PosixPath('/Users/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.venv/lib/python3.13')\ndoes not contain src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py — default root resolution is wrong;\nexpected Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4] from __main__.py\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe reconciler's `main()` default repo-root fallback (in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, when `--repo-root`/`REBAR_ROOT` are absent) derives the root as `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]`. Under an **editable** install `__file__` is `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, so `parents[4]` is the repo root. Under a **non-editable** install `__file__` is `<venv>/lib/pythonX/site-packages/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, so `parents[4]` is `<venv>/lib/pythonX` — not a checkout. `test_reconcile_main.py::_assert_resolved_repo_root` asserts the resolved default contains `src/rebar/...`, which cannot hold once installed.\n\nUnlike the release-packaging tests fixed under the parent ticket (test-side path derivation), this is a **production** behavior: the reconciler's default repo-root under a non-editable install is a checkout path that does not exist.\n\n## Fix direction (BEHAVIOR — needs decision)\n\nDecide what the reconciler's default repo root should be when installed non-editably (e.g. require `--repo-root`/`REBAR_ROOT`, fall back to CWD, or error clearly), and update `_default_repo_root()` and its test accordingly. Behavior-altering -> design decision.\n\n## Evidence\n- Mirror run 33299427686: `sweep (macos, full suite)` job 99224621948 (4x), `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` job 99224621821 (6x).\n- Also failing in the pre-fix run 33285143350 macOS leg (pre-existing, was masked by the collection error).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `test_reconcile_main.py` repo-root resolution assertions pass under both editable and non-editable installs.\n- [ ] The reconciler's default repo-root behavior under a non-editable install is defined and documented (no silent resolution into the venv tree).","id":"c0b9-33b0-f968-450d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-portability","reconciler"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler default repo-root fallback (__main__.py parents[4]) assumes an editable checkout; wrong under non-editable install"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788078145368473209,"uuid":"ae3c72cd-3ec6-4b66-a331-122614e3433a"}